{"name":"Clover","hex":"#008f00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Clover","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Clover"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clover","blocks":[{"text":"Clovers, also called trefoils, are plants of the genus Trifolium. They are herbaceous plants growing up to 30 cm (12 in) tall. The leaves are usually trifoliate and the small flowers are reddish to white or yellow. Related genera with similar common names include Melilotus and Medicago (burclover)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg/330px-79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clover","wikidata":"Q101538"},{"title":"Clover (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Clover was an American country rock band formed in Mill Valley, California and active from 1967 to 1978. Clover are best known as the backing band for Elvis Costello's 1977 debut album My Aim Is True, and for its members going on to greater success with Huey Lewis and the News, the Doobie Brothers, and Lucinda Williams."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clover_(band)","wikidata":"Q5135860"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/250px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/500px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/250px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrifolium_dubium_RF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org